# API (NestJS)

Read [docs/apps/api.md](../../docs/apps/api.md) first.

## Layout

- One domain per folder under `apps/api/src/` (e.g. `registration/`, `voting/`)
- `*.module.ts` for Nest modules; `*.controller.ts` for routes; `*.service.ts` for business logic
- Register controllers and providers in `app.module.ts` (flat module — no feature modules for most domains)
- Shared cross-cutting: `auth/`, `mailer/`, `tokens/`, `file-upload/`, `background/`, `event/`

## Models

- Import Sequelize models from `@coolestprojects/database` — do not define models in `apps/api`
- Register models in `SequelizeModule.forRootAsync` and `forFeature` in `app.module.ts`
- Rebuild database package after model changes: `npm run build --workspace=packages/database`

## Auth

- `AuthModule` provides `AUTH_JWT` and `VOTING_JWT` (separate secrets: `JWT_KEY`, `VOTING_KEY`)
- Passport strategies in `auth/` (`jwt.strategy.ts`, `jwt-voting.strategy.ts`, `file-sign.strategy.ts`)
- Voting routes live on `VotingController` at root paths (`/auth/login`, `/projects`, etc.)

## Conventions

- Keep controllers thin; put logic in services
- Global `InfoInterceptor` is registered via `APP_INTERCEPTOR` — responses include info metadata
- CLI commands via `nestjs-command` in `cli.ts`; seed with `npm run seed-db`
- Env via `@nestjs/config` (`ConfigModule.forRoot({ isGlobal: true })`)

## Tests

- Spec files colocated (`*.spec.ts`); use `@nestjs/testing` patterns
